      "created_at": "2025-11-07T11:30:44.663Z",
      "cooked": "<blockquote>\n<p><a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/vigneshwar_2006\">@Vigneshwar_2006</a><br>\nThis usually happens when you are inside a <strong>read-only directory</strong> like <code>/opt/se2001</code>.<br>\nYou cannot create or edit files there.</p>\n<p>Try this method instead:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>Go to your <strong>home directory</strong></p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-auto\">cd ~/se2001\n\n</code></pre>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Make a new folder for your problem (for example):</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-auto\">mkdir BPT3_problem_1\ncd BPT3_problem_1\n\n</code></pre>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Then create your script:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-auto\">nano script.sh\n\n</code></pre>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>After saving, make it executable:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-auto\">chmod +x script.sh\n\n</code></pre>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Finally, run your evaluation:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-auto\">synchro eval\n\n</code></pre>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p>This will solve the “directory not writable” issue. You can only edit inside your <strong>home directory</strong>, not inside <code>/opt/se2001</code>.</p>\n</blockquote>",
